{"text": "Geoffrey G. Burr\n\n(b) (6)\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nJanuary 2017 \u2014 Present\nSpecial Assistant to the Secretary, U.S. Department of Labor\nPolitical Appointee \u2014 Senior Executive Service, Washington, DC\n> Served as Chief of Staff-Designee to Secretary of Labor Nominee Andrew Puzder\n> Executed DOL \u201cBeachhead Team\u201d strategy and transition beginning on Inauguration Day in regular consultation with White\nHouse Legislative Affairs and Domestic Policy Council staff\n> Served as confirmation \u201cSherpa\u201d for Nominee Puzder and continue a role on Sherpa team for Nominee R. Alexander Acosta\n> Implemented Administration agenda and policy goals at the Department as directed by senior White House staff\n\nNovember 2016 \u2014 January 2017\nLead Congressional Liaison (\u201cSherpa\u201d) for Transportation Secretary Nominee Elaine L. Chao\nPresidential Transition, Washington, DC\n> Led confirmation team charged with managing the successful confirmation of Elaine Chao as Transportation Secretary\n> Prepared nominee for confirmation hearing; staffed nominee for Senate visits; responsible for managing issue briefings and\nhearing strategy\n> Managed Office of Government Ethics, background check and Commerce Committee processes for nominee\n\nSeptember 2015 \u2014 June 2016\nVice President, Government Affairs\nCablevision Systems Corporation, New York\n> Developed and managed political and legislative strategy for fifth largest cable and internet provider in the United\nStates serving New York, New Jersey, Connecticut and Pennsylvania\n> Oversaw and managed state and local field teams responsible with managing key state, local and NYC City Council\nrelationships and securing and renewing hundreds of local cable franchise agreements\n> Developed and executed company\u2019s federal, state and local PAC contribution and charitable contribution strategies;\nbuilt and strengthened company relationships with public officials and communities\n> Represented company\u2019s interests before federal and state regulatory agencies to support key business priorities,\npositioned the company favorably and ensured no competitive harms\n> Prepared senior executives for testimony on behalf of the company and for meetings with key elected officials and\ngovernment agencies\n> Managed relationships with influential third party organizations, business groups and charitable organizations\n\nNovember 2008 \u2014 September 2015\nVice President, Government Affairs\nAssociated Builders and Contractors, Inc., Washington, DC\n> Oversaw and managed government relations operation of $18 million revenue national trade association representing\n22,000 firms in 74 chapters nationwide\n\n> Managed and developed strategy for association\u2019s state and local affairs programs, which resulted in ABC\u2019s signature\nlegislation, the Government Neutrality in Contracting Act being passed into law in 23 states during tenure.\n> Managed federal political action committee (ABC PAC) which raised and distributed approximately $2 million per\nelection cycle and the Free Enterprise Alliance, a soft-money issue advocacy operation\n\n> Served as association\u2019s chief lobbyist and advocate on Capitol Hill with oversight of a legislative department with\nparticular focus on labor, tax and small business issues\n> Managed association\u2019s regulatory affairs department, including advocacy at federal agencies; extensive experience\nwith the federal rulemaking process\n> Oversaw association\u2019s legal affairs, including management of the Construction Legal Rights Foundation, a legal trust\nthat supports cases of national significance to the association\u2019s interests",
